{"`end` is computed from `slotStartTime` instead of `slotEndTime`, making it identical to `start`. This means the working-hours boundary check never validates the slot's end time \u2014 slots that extend past working hours will be treated as available.": 0.9892053604125977, "Dayjs objects compared by reference (`===`) \u2014 this is always `false`. Use `.isSame()` to compare the underlying time values. Without this fix, date overrides representing \"unavailable all day\" (start === end) will be silently ignored.": 0.9771900773048401, "`override.timeZone` is optional on the `TimeRange` type. If it's `undefined`, `dayjs(...).tz(undefined)` will produce an incorrect UTC offset. Fall back to `organizerTimeZone` (already available in the enclosing `getSlots` scope) to avoid a silent miscalculation.": 0.9720787405967712}